            <ArticleTitle>Latex Safe at School: A Student-Centered Approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-345</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1942602X17715495</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Providing a safe environment for students at risk for anaphylaxis from a latex allergy requires care coordination and collaboration of all members of the school community. Strategies for allergy management include educating the school community, identifying potential exposure to latex, preparing to respond in an emergency, and creating a plan for the future. With the student at the center of sound planning, the school can provide a secure and healthy environment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
